{"op":"add","path":"/elements/method-text","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"content":"This analysis used 36 monthly plan-level records (Starter, Pro, Enterprise) spanning the full year. Net new MRR per month was computed as new MRR plus expansion MRR minus churn MRR, then summed across plans. The jump month was identified as the calendar month with the largest month-over-month increase in that aggregate. The waterfall decomposes the jump into its three components. A step-change test assessed whether the jump represented a persistent level shift. The plan attribution compares each plan's contribution in the jump month against the prior month.","variant":"body"},"children":[]}}
